cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use CorpusMind Lens in your research, please cite it using this
  metadata (BibTeX or the CSL variant your publisher prefers).
title: >-
  CorpusMind Lens: a local-first, AI-native visual and multimodal
  corpus-analysis environment
abstract: >-
  CorpusMind Lens turns sets of images — with or without accompanying text —
  into publication-ready, statistically grounded, framework-lensed discourse
  analysis. It implements a five-dimension visual annotation framework
  (Cohn 2013; Kress & van Leeuwen 2006; Bateman 2008; Bordwell & Thompson
  2013; McCloud 1993; Barthes 1977; Royce 2007) and applies the full corpus-
  linguistics measurement battery — frequency, diversity, n-grams,
  co-occurrence association, keyness with paired significance and effect
  sizes, dispersion, and concordance — over visual annotation sequences, for
  the first time giving image corpora the same evidentiary apparatus corpus
  linguistics has always demanded of text.
